"""
GNM head model backend - identity/expression/pose parameters, ARKit-52 +
FACS + semantic blend-shape tables, and the glTF exporter.

This module is UI-framework agnostic (no glfw/imgui/moderngl/PySide6 here):
it only depends on numpy + the internal ``gnm`` package (with a mock
icosphere fallback via trimesh when ``gnm`` isn't importable, so this module
still loads on machines without the proprietary GNM package). The Qt/OpenGL
viewer lives in :mod:`synclip.tools.gnm_head_viewer` and imports everything
it needs from here.

Ported from the original standalone ``viewer.py`` GNM debug tool with its
data tables, blend-shape math, and glTF export kept byte-for-byte identical
in behaviour - only the glfw/imgui/moderngl-only bits (window, camera,
immediate-mode UI) were dropped, since those move to the Qt UI module and
reuse the same orbit-camera + mesh-render conventions as
:mod:`synclip.ui.mesh_renderer`.

- Full res 17821 verts, quads 17662 -> tris 35324
- glTF: shared vertices, POSITION/NORMAL/TEXCOORD_0, 106 morph targets with
  official ARKit + FACS + semantic names, deltas per vertex
"""

